## net.sf.trove4j:trove4j 3.0.3 — LGPL-2.1

The 2022 engine's `ObjectInfo` keeps its robots in a
`gnu.trove.map.hash.TIntObjectHashMap`, and `robotsArray()` is that map's
`values(V[])` — a high-index-to-low walk over the open-addressed table. That
order is **read by a rule**: the global CHARGE anomaly sorts the board's droids
and destroys the top 5 %, and a stable sort over a differently-ordered input
kills different robots. Measured over 900 recorded dumps, 51-58 % of CHARGE
rounds contain at least one tie that the iteration order decides.

`src/battlecode/years/bc22/trove.nim` therefore reproduces that **observable
iteration order**: the open-addressing scheme, the auto-compacting rehash, the
tombstone history and the capacity ladder, hand-written in Nim from the
documented algorithm and verified bit-for-bit against the jar's own trove
classes. **No trove source or bytecode is vendored, compiled or copied**; the
class files reached only the CI-only oracle jar's classpath and never any
image. The dependency and its licence are recorded here because reproducing a
library's iteration order derives from its *behaviour*, and this repository
says so plainly rather than leaving it implicit.

